{
	"_readme": [
		"The whole quest, played WELL, end to end - and the only gate that proves the fights, the",
		"levels and the Item command all work on the shipped data rather than on a fixture.",
		"",
		"Every battle wait below is derived, not guessed. data/combat/quest_combat.tres gives a",
		"72-frame swing, an 84-frame enemy telegraph, a 24-frame window and a 45-frame message, so",
		"one round is 246 ticks from confirm back to the menu; a QA `press` costs 3 frames and a",
		"`wait(N)` costs N+1. The presses land mid-window with about twelve frames of slack either",
		"side. RETUNE THE TIMING AND THESE NUMBERS ALL MOVE - recompute them from that file.",
		"",
		"Two rules of this harness show up everywhere below. A leg is held until a WALL or a BODY",
		"stops it, never for a counted number of tiles. And an arriving hold carries the player",
		"onward into the next map, which is used deliberately here: one held key takes us out of",
		"the hollow, across the village and into the gate.",
		"",
		"A fight adds a third: it stops the player wherever they stood, which is rarely a tile",
		"centre - so every leg that follows a battle re-anchors on a wall before it goes anywhere",
		"near a one-tile gap."
	],
